{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Wisdom has built her house</b> — like <b>בנות צעדה</b> (Genesis 13:8: \"there was strife\")." "<b>She has hewn her pillars</b> — a borrowed usage from hewers of stone. The meaning concerns the setting of the pillars by hewing and by other forms of preparation. It is also possible to interpret that she said <b>חכמות</b> (wisdoms) to indicate that Wisdom built her house from seven wisdoms, and this is the meaning of <b>חצבה עמודיה שבעה</b> (she has hewn her seven pillars) — and they are the pillars of the house, and it is the explanation of the statement <b>חכמות בנתה ביתה</b>. And <b>בית</b> is in the feminine, or <b>עמודיה שבעה</b> — the seven pillars of Wisdom, and the pillars are the seven wisdoms upon which the house of Wisdom is established. And there are interpreters: these seven are on other matters, and each chooses for himself, and the truth will point its way."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:40.029169164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}